{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de4b8aa20fc16230f14b52", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Oscillations - Test 3", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969cc"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92968b8", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967b7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e8587"], "question": {"text": "For a periodic motion represented by the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>sin&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>cos&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></math> the amplitude of the motion is"}, "options": [{"id": "7e4e7e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967b8"}, {"id": "d32ea7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967b9"}, {"id": "d336e4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967ba"}, {"id": "89fe09", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967bb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967bc", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b85"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d42"], "question": {"text": "<p>A mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is connected to a spring. The potential energy curve of the simple harmonic motion executed by the system is shown in the figure. A simple pendulum of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> has the same period of oscillation as the spring system. What is the value of acceleration due to gravity on the planet where these experiments are performed ?</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ffacb5fab-ab24-4c94-b446-ba789f5d0c92-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 380px; height: 324px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "dc1dc4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967bd"}, {"id": "db6e3b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967be"}, {"id": "8b694c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967bf"}, {"id": "87bea1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967c0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967c1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee5"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5df5"], "question": {"text": "A simple pendulum oscillating in air has period <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> . The bob of the pendulum is completely immersed in a non-viscous liquid. The density of the liquid is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math> of the material of the bob. If the bob is inside liquid all the time, its period of oscillation in this liquid is:"}, "options": [{"id": "0a9687", "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967c2"}, {"id": "dc750a", "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967c3"}, {"id": "af9366", "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967c4"}, {"id": "0caaf8", "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967c5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967c6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4764"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b471a"], "question": {"text": "When a particle of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;is attached to a vertical spring of spring constant&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math>&nbsp;and released, its motion, is described by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#969;t</mi></math>, where &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math>&#39; is measured from the lower end of upstretched spring. Then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi></math>&nbsp;is :"}, "options": [{"id": "6bb772", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967c7"}, {"id": "1daaec", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967c8"}, {"id": "830646", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967c9"}, {"id": "3436de", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967ca"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967cb", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3e"], "question": {"text": "The equation of a particle executing simple harmonic motion is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, the speed of particle will be (Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "c0dd27", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>157</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967cc"}, {"id": "70f0c8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967cd"}, {"id": "12dee3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>272</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967ce"}, {"id": "00a7c3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>314</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967cf"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967d0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b85"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b53"], "question": {"text": "For what value of displacement the kinetic energy and potential energy of a simple harmonic oscillation become equal?"}, "options": [{"id": "87187b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967d1"}, {"id": "680648", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mi>A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967d2"}, {"id": "b7a36c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967d3"}, {"id": "fb711f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967d4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967d5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee5"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d33"], "question": {"text": "A simple pendulum of length $1 \\mathrm{~m}$ is oscillating with an angular frequency $10 \\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{s}$. The support of the pendulum starts oscillating up and down with a small angular frequency of $1 \\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{s}$ and an amplitude of $10^{-2} \\mathrm{~m}$. The relative change in the angular frequency of the pendulum is best given by :"}, "options": [{"id": "fc9758", "text": "$10^{-3} \\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967d6"}, {"id": "d65806", "text": "$1 \\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967d7"}, {"id": "86187d", "text": "$10^{-1} \\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967d8"}, {"id": "92b081", "text": "$10^{-5} \\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967d9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967da", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4764"], "concepts": ["6117b607478ae845c43c631c"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements:<br />Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>: A second&#39;s pendulum has a time period of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> second.</p><p>Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math>: It takes precisely one second to move between the two extreme positions. In the light of the above statements,</p><p>choose the correct answer from the options given below</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "2ea912", "text": "Statement&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is false but Statement&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967db"}, {"id": "069262", "text": "Both Statement&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> and Statement&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967dc"}, {"id": "d569c5", "text": "Both Statement&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> and Statement&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> are False", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967dd"}, {"id": "533474", "text": "Statement&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is true but Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math>&nbsp;is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967de"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967df", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d2a"], "question": {"text": "A particle executes S.H.M., the graph of velocity as a function of displacement is :"}, "options": [{"id": "7c4128", "text": "a circle", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967e0"}, {"id": "ba4fde", "text": "a helix", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967e1"}, {"id": "eae75f", "text": "a parabola", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967e2"}, {"id": "705188", "text": "an ellipse", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967e3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967e4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b85"], "concepts": ["6117b90767dbe2603c3e8f87"], "question": {"text": "For a body executing S.H.M. :<br />(a) Potential energy is always equal to its&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br />(b) Average potential and kinetic energy over any given time interval are always equal.<br />(c) Sum of the kinetic and potential energy at any point of time is constant.<br />(d) Average&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;in one time period is equal to average potential energy in one time period.<br />Choose the most appropriate option from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "a25255", "text": "(c) and (d)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967e5"}, {"id": "02e71b", "text": "only (c)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967e6"}, {"id": "b9a5a4", "text": "only (b)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967e7"}, {"id": "309d1e", "text": "(b) and (c)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967e8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967e9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee5"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5df5"], "question": {"text": "Two blocks of masses $m$ and $M,(M \\gt m)$, are placed on a frictionless table as shown in figure. A massless spring with spring constant k is attached with the lower block. If the system is slightly displaced and released then<br/>($\\mu=$ coefficient of friction between the two blocks)<br/><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F3MCVr793g00YQtaQ76itGjnEmQr0P0HoNmi5TKwW0ic.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>(A) The time period of small oscillation of the two blocks is $\\mathrm{T}=2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{(\\mathrm{~m}+\\mathrm{M})}{\\mathrm{k}}}$<br/>(B) The acceleration of the blocks is $\\mathrm{a}=\\frac{\\mathrm{kx}}{\\mathrm{M}+\\mathrm{m}}$ ($\\mathrm{x}=$ displacement of the blocks from the mean position)<br/>(C) The magnitude of the frictional force on the upper block is $\\frac{m \\mu|x|}{M+m}$<br/>(D) The maximum amplitude of the upper block, if it does not slip, is $\\frac{\\mu(M+m) g}{k}$<br/>(E) Maximum frictional force can be $\\mu(\\mathrm{M}+\\mathrm{m}) \\mathrm{g}$.<br/>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "4aff43", "text": "A, B, D Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967ea"}, {"id": "1ec915", "text": "B, C, D Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967eb"}, {"id": "99c1d5", "text": "C, D, E Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967ec"}, {"id": "b443c1", "text": "A, B, C Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967ed"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967ee", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4764"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b471a"], "question": {"text": "<p>For a simple harmonic motion in a mass spring system shown, the surface is frictionless. When the mass of the block is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>, the angular frequency is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. When the mass block is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> the angular frequency is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math> is :</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F861dba8a-dda9-4a16-b006-5dccd6d5693e-21218936-f367-42ee-a85b-3926958fb97f-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 79px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "ff0624", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967ef"}, {"id": "f14d6c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967f0"}, {"id": "95fb27", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967f1"}, {"id": "c0be98", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967f2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967f3", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e8587"], "question": {"text": "A particle is executing simple harmonic motion with time period 2 s and amplitude 1 cm . If D and d are the total distance and displacement covered by the particle in 12.5 s , then $\\frac{\\mathrm{D}}{\\mathrm{d}}$ is"}, "options": [{"id": "098b0b", "text": "$\\frac{16}{5}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967f4"}, {"id": "bfcc64", "text": "$10$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967f5"}, {"id": "8fd54c", "text": "$\\frac{15}{4}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967f6"}, {"id": "10e037", "text": "$25$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967f7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967f8", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b85"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d42"], "question": {"text": "A particle is executing simple harmonic motion (SHM). The ratio of potential energy and kinetic energy of the particle when its displacement is half of its amplitude will be"}, "options": [{"id": "a58884", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967f9"}, {"id": "16ca81", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967fa"}, {"id": "abbb35", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967fb"}, {"id": "3c420f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967fc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967fd", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee5"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5df5"], "question": {"text": "The displacement of simple harmonic oscillator after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;seconds starting from its mean position is equal to half of its amplitude. The time period of harmonic motion is"}, "options": [{"id": "5078f5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967fe"}, {"id": "654e2b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967ff"}, {"id": "bfda66", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296800"}, {"id": "b31d2c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296801"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296802", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4764"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b471a"], "question": {"text": "The amplitude of a mass-spring system, which is executing simple harmonic motion decreases with time. If mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>, Decay constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> then how much time is required for the amplitude of the system to drop to half of its initial value? <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>693</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "330ee1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>34</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>65</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296803"}, {"id": "715e16", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>17</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296804"}, {"id": "0ea55d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>034</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296805"}, {"id": "7d7a13", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296806"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296807", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b85"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b53"], "question": {"text": "A particle undergoing simple harmonic motion has time\n\ndependent displacement given by $x(t)=\\mathrm{A} \\sin \\frac{\\pi t}{90}$. The ratio of kinetic to potential energy of this particle at $\\mathrm{t}=210 \\mathrm{~s}$ will be"}, "options": [{"id": "263c0b", "text": "$\\frac{1}{9}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296808"}, {"id": "006b67", "text": "1", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296809"}, {"id": "8648a8", "text": "2", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d929680a"}, {"id": "0405de", "text": "$\\frac{1}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d929680b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d929680c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3e"], "question": {"text": "<p>In a linear Simple Harmonic Motion (SHM)</p><p>(A) Restoring force is directly proportional to the displacement.</p><p>(B) The acceleration and displacement are opposite in direction.</p><p>(C) The velocity is maximum at mean position.</p><p>(D) The acceleration is minimum at extreme points.</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "afa132", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d929680d"}, {"id": "763e6a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d929680e"}, {"id": "392e74", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d929680f"}, {"id": "f88853", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296810"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296811", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee5"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5df5"], "question": {"text": "A particle executes simple harmonic motion with an amplitude of <math><mn>5</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math> . When the particle is at <math><mn>4</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math> from the mean position, the magnitude of its velocity in <math><mi>S</mi><mi>I</mi></math> units is equal to that of its acceleration. Then, its periodic time in seconds is:"}, "options": [{"id": "bf957f", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296812"}, {"id": "824fc4", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>π</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296813"}, {"id": "db1c49", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296814"}, {"id": "0603e9", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>π</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296815"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296816", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4764"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b471a"], "question": {"text": "<p>Two identical springs of spring constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></math> are attached to a block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> and to fixed support (see figure). When the mass is displaced from equilibrium position on either side, it executes simple harmonic motion. The time period of oscillations of this system is :</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F08d637f9-d45d-4be0-929e-d4edde9e17ab-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 336px; height: 95px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "b4b363", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296817"}, {"id": "4f003c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296818"}, {"id": "fcbc27", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d9296819"}, {"id": "23968d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d929681a"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:31.106Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:31.106Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969ca"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969c7", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969a4", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3e"], "question": {"text": "A particle is doing simple harmonic motion of amplitude $0.06 \\mathrm{~m}$ and time period $3.14 \\mathrm{~s}$. The maximum velocity of the particle is _______ $\\mathrm{cm} / \\mathrm{s}$."}, "options": [{"id": "069551", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969a5"}, {"id": "9dd020", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969a6"}, {"id": "a48368", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969a7"}, {"id": "d95fc6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969a8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969a9", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee5"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5df5"], "question": {"text": "The metallic bob of simple pendulum has the relative density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>. The time period of this pendulum is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. If the metallic bob is immersed in water, then the new time period becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> will be _____ ."}, "options": [{"id": "4685d5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969aa"}, {"id": "6fe3f1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969ab"}, {"id": "313b83", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969ac"}, {"id": "1578ab", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969ad"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969ae", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b85"], "concepts": ["6117b90767dbe2603c3e8f87"], "question": {"text": "A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is hanging from a spring of force constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The mass is pulled slightly downward and released so that it executes free simple harmonic motion with time period <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The time when the kinetic energy and potential energy of the system will&nbsp;become equal, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is ________."}, "options": [{"id": "2288f6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969af"}, {"id": "12701f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969b0"}, {"id": "1b0b69", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969b1"}, {"id": "1e43a4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969b2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969b3", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4764"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b471a"], "question": {"text": "<p>In the figure given below. a block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>490</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;placed on a frictionless table is connected with two springs having same spring constant (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>). If the block is horizontally displaced through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> then the number of complete oscillations it will make in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math> seconds will be ______.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fdef3d0ba-9e6a-4709-805f-bdce7f881a7a-9896057.PNG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 343px; height: 225px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "5117c2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969b4"}, {"id": "d82253", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969b5"}, {"id": "7abd90", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969b6"}, {"id": "b331e0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969b7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969b8", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["6117b64c478ae845c43c6818"], "question": {"text": "A particle performs simple harmonic motion with amplitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>. Its speed is increased to three times at an instant when its displacement is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. The new amplitude of motion is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is _____."}, "options": [{"id": "a747d7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969b9"}, {"id": "7be438", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969ba"}, {"id": "4d9649", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969bb"}, {"id": "cecae7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969bc"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:31.203Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:31.203Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4f872ee0e063d92969cb"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:13:30.463Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04:58:01.862Z", "testType": "PYQs as Chapter Tests", "isResumeBufferAllowed": true, "enableAccessibility": true, "maxAttemptableQuestion": 25, "analysisVideoThumbnail": "", "analysisVideoThumbnailDark": "", "shortTitle": "", "subjectDetails": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "title": "Physics", "shortName": "Phy"}], "testTimerType": "mm", "isMarkForReviewAvailable": true}, "temporaryTestDetail": {"_id": "6a4a1e8d4e144b2381779d74", "testId": "69de4b8aa20fc16230f14b52", "userId": "6914cc9c4d7566258ee3a8fd", "startedAt": "2026-07-05T09:06:21.044Z", "lastAttemptedSection": null, "totalTimeLeft": 50, "bonusAttempt": false, "sections": [{"sectionId": "69de4f872ee0e063d92968b8", "questions": [{"questionId": "69de4f872ee0e063d92967b7", "markedOptions": [], "inputValue": null, "timeTaken": 0, "timeLeftWhenAttempted": null, "status": "notVisited", "_i